{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create","id":1459189,"title":"What CofD Game would you create?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-07T14:25:05-07:00","id":1459189,"title":"What CofD Game would you create?","content":"i'm curious,if you had to pitch a new cofd game,or create one entirely from scratch what would it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T14:45:11-07:00","id":1459195,"title":"","content":"Aliens? Time travelers?<br /> Adventurers (as in, the dungeon-crawl genre)?<br /> <br /> Maybe a redux of the Ferals (Changing Breeds) and the Possessed (Inferno) from 1E. Though in my current headcanon the former are uplifted animals and the true identity of the \u2018planetary angels of Gaia itself\u2019 mentioned in Shunned By the Moon, and the latter are a subset of \u2018fallen\u2019 Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T14:53:14-07:00","id":1459197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1459195#post1459195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aliens? Time travelers?<br /> Adventurers (as in, the dungeon-crawl genre)?<br /> <br /> Maybe a redux of the Ferals (Changing Breeds) and the Possessed (Inferno) from 1E. Though in my current headcanon the former are uplifted animals and the true identity of the \u2018planetary angels of Gaia itself\u2019 mentioned in Shunned By the Moon, and the latter are a subset of \u2018fallen\u2019 Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating ideas. I've been craving some of that stuff for a while now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T17:36:26-07:00","id":1459220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1459195#post1459195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aliens? Time travelers?<br /> Adventurers (as in, the dungeon-crawl genre)?<br /> <br /> Maybe a redux of the Ferals (Changing Breeds) and the Possessed (Inferno) from 1E. Though in my current headcanon the former are uplifted animals and the true identity of the \u2018planetary angels of Gaia itself\u2019 mentioned in Shunned By the Moon, and the latter are a subset of \u2018fallen\u2019 Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time-traveling alien dungeon-crawlers possessed by demonic shapechangers? Sounds doable? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T17:40:25-07:00","id":1459221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1459220#post1459220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time-traveling alien dungeon-crawlers possessed by demonic shapechangers? Sounds doable? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well we can have Visitors (1E Immortals/2E Mummy) raiding Mummy tombs\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T17:46:49-07:00","id":1459222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1459220#post1459220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time-traveling alien dungeon-crawlers possessed by demonic shapechangers? Sounds doable? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>i'm in, what would be the title?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T18:53:34-07:00","id":1459228,"title":"","content":"To build on what others mentioned above, since it's actually pretty close to something I proposed in another thread:<br /> <br /> <b>Alien: The Other</b><br /> <br /> Characters are not necessarily from space (although that is definitely one of the available options), but could also be displaced from another time, an alternate reality, or another plane of existence. The thing that matters is that despite existing on the CofD version of Earth, they're not actually <i>from</i> the world they now inhabit. One way or another, it's strange to them.<br /> <br /> The reason they wound up on CofD Earth could vary as well, but the important thing is that they can't go back. They could be here entirely on accident, they could have willingly come here to explore but became stuck, sent here in exile as a form of punishment, or they could be refugees who view CofD Earth as &quot;safer&quot; than their home.<br /> <br /> Antagonists could be other Aliens who have come to hunt them down, or are competing for the same territory, resources, or people that the player Aliens have connections with. Or human/supernatural organizations who are aware of the Aliens and want them gone.<br /> <br /> Power sets could in theory depend on what type of Alien the character is. If you're from space, then you have different biology from humans, and your abilities would reflect that. From another time, you have access to advanced technology and knowledge. Alternate reality, your existence causes CofD Earth to &quot;break&quot; around you, allowing you to twist things in your favor. Another plane of existence, you could have abilities that reflect your true nature, such as Numina for an Alien whose natural state is Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26615,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26615-runomai","user":"RuNoMai","date":". 09-07-2021, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26615-runomai","name":"RuNoMai","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T22:03:20-07:00","id":1459254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create#post1459189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'm curious,if you had to pitch a new cofd game,or create one entirely from scratch what would it be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan on doing the SCP Foundation and currently have Pok\u00e9mon almost done. I also have a half-way through adaptation of the Lantern Corps somewhere on my PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T06:49:42-07:00","id":1459294,"title":"","content":"&quot;Essence of Darkness.&quot; A lighter, more accessible variant of the CofD, streamlining and cutting mechanics and settings down to essential elements. Using Deviant's power building as a foundation and some of the other build-a-thing stuff, Contagion Chronicle crossover material, etc, to create a toolkit-approach-ground-up take on the core ideas of the CofD as a whole.<br /> <br /> By necessity you'd have to cut a lot of setting material to collapse everyone into a build-your-own-human-turned-monster-in-a-secret-occult-horror-world so I'd envision it as a sibling game line, quasi-separated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 09-08-2021, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T04:14:07-07:00","id":1460015,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't create a new one; I'd create supplements for the existing ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","user":"Vintervalpen","date":". 09-15-2021, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12103-vintervalpen","name":"Vintervalpen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T08:55:15-07:00","id":1460046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1459294#post1459294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Essence of Darkness.&quot; A lighter, more accessible variant of the CofD, streamlining and cutting mechanics and settings down to essential elements. Using Deviant's power building as a foundation and some of the other build-a-thing stuff, Contagion Chronicle crossover material, etc, to create a toolkit-approach-ground-up take on the core ideas of the CofD as a whole.<br /> <br /> By necessity you'd have to cut a lot of setting material to collapse everyone into a build-your-own-human-turned-monster-in-a-secret-occult-horror-world so I'd envision it as a sibling game line, quasi-separated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could actually really dig a distilled/Chronicles-lite product.<br /> <br /> FOr those saying Alien, again I say wait for the Clade Companion. Once you apply the Outsider Form to Deviant's themes and possibilities, it really solidly covers a lot of the narratives you'd want from the subject matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T11:49:41-07:00","id":1460071,"title":"","content":"Such amazing suggestions everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T06:48:01-07:00","id":1460424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1460046#post1460046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could actually really dig a distilled/Chronicles-lite product.<br /> <br /> FOr those saying Alien, again I say wait for the Clade Companion. Once you apply the Outsider Form to Deviant's themes and possibilities, it really solidly covers a lot of the narratives you'd want from the subject matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; Deviant really does seem to be the \u201c\u2026and the rest\u201d gameline. Not to say that there's nothing else to be done; just that it's <i>really hard</i> to think of anything not covered (directly or adjacently) by the existing eleven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T12:44:08-07:00","id":1460455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1460424#post1460424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah; Deviant really does seem to be the \u201c\u2026and the rest\u201d gameline. Not to say that there's nothing else to be done; just that it's <i>really hard</i> to think of anything not covered (directly or adjacently) by the existing eleven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't neccesarily say that it's supposed to be &quot;the rest&quot;, because Deviant has a lot more specificity than that-it's too red blooded, too interpersonally connected, and too centered on conspiracies, as a few short hand examples(there's many more), to be &quot;The Rest&quot; gameline. Beast is more the &quot;And the Rest&quot; gameline than Deviant is. And I'd still contend that niether of those is &quot;the rest&quot; gameline, becuase a &quot;the rest&quot; is basically a GURPs game and I don't know anyone who wants to make anything so flavorless and boring.<br /> <br /> But if you think about the sort of directly alien* stories out there that you would want to see in a Chronicles of Darkness perspective**, a lot of them neatly line up with the Deviant model, including blending in imperfectly, possibly having strange powers or urges that occasionally get out of control, organizations keeping an eye out for them to advance in myriad ways, and aliens running or fighting back, either as advance troops or spies or just through the dumb luck of being there, all the while developing close connections that allow them to slip by and work things out while they're doing whatever it is they need to do ,and a whole lot more. THe Outsider Form allows for the one missing thing, being Alien-or-Other being afflicted with humanity for [insert purpose here] by [insert offending party here], but not being wholly human in the process.<br /> <br /> Hell, with other Forms, you can even do The Cat From Outer Space, Dogstar, or Flight of the Navigator.<br /> <br /> I will say this, I didn't write the Outsider Form to try and end the requests for an Alien splat (That's impossible in any scenario but an Alien book being announced, because People Be Like That, and also that would be a dick move-I'm not here to shut down fansplats)-but I <i>did</i> write it with the hope that Alien pitches after the fact might be <i>really good</i> to warrant the jump.<br /> <br /> *So no Mars Attack or Independence Day.<br /> **Because we have Changeling and Demon for a lot of the stories you might want to already tell, and Deviant rounds out the lot. If there's an alien narrative you want to tell in Chronicles after the fact, it's a very <i>niche</i> story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-19T15:42:29-07:00","id":1460475,"title":"","content":"Two points: first, I recall the original Deviant developer saying that one of his design goals was to make Deviant so flexible that it <i>could</i> be used as a sort of catch-all for the various monster types that don't fit the other splats. The fact that it can handle everything from the Invisible Man and the Island of Doctor Moreau to Robocop and Buffy the Vampire Slayer is a testament to this. <br /> <br /> Second, a well-designed gameline <i>can</i> largely cover the ground claimed by a fansplat. I definitely see Deviant doing this with at least three of them: Princess, Alien, and Genius. However, I don't see this as an attempt to \u201csquash\u201d the fansplats; they can continue to exist as unofficial alternate takes on the monster types they deal with, and they're exactly as valid <i>after</i> Deviant came out as they were <i>before</i> it did. <br /> <br /> IMHO, Deviant's role in the Chronicles of Darkness is similar to the role that Exigents play in Exalted: want to play a monster that doesn't fit into any of the other ten monster types, but <i>without</i> having to build a whole new fansplat in order to do it? Chances are <i>really good</i> that you'll be able to frame it in a way that fits into Deviant. <i>That's</i> what I meant by Deviant being \u201cand the rest\u201d.<br /> <br /> Bringing this back on topic for the thread: the versatility of Deviant means that going forward, the motive for a fansplat is no longer going to be \u201chere's this monster type that doesn't have a place in the Chronicles of Darkness; what would be an interesting way to bring it in?\u201d but rather \u201chere's a type of story that's suitable for the Chronicles of Darkness but doesn't currently have anything to cover it in the existing gamelines; what monster type could we use to address it?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-20-2021, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T21:07:14-07:00","id":1460606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1460475#post1460475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, a well-designed gameline <i>can</i> largely cover the ground claimed by a fansplat. I definitely see Deviant doing this with at least three of them: Princess, Alien, and Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite see how Deviant covers the ground claimed by Genius or Princess. The themes of Genius are covered by Mage - in both games you play someone with incredible power, but not the wisdom to use it well. That's not a natural fit for Deviant, where the guiding metaphor is &quot;powers are a handicap&quot; and the main enemies are organizations of ordinary people.<br /> <br /> And with Princess - well, the biggest knock on <i>that</i> fansplat is that it doesn't fit the Chronicles setting at all, and it's partly justified, too. Whereas Deviant, with its half-broken protagonists and occult conspirators with nefarious plans, is probably the official game closest to the tone of the original blue book. The only overlap I see is that both games can do some kinds of superhero stories, and even there the similarities aren't that close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-20T22:27:54-07:00","id":1460613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1460606#post1460606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't quite see how Deviant covers the ground claimed by Genius or Princess. The themes of Genius are covered by Mage - in both games you play someone with incredible power, but not the wisdom to use it well. That's not a natural fit for Deviant, where the guiding metaphor is &quot;powers are a handicap&quot; and the main enemies are organizations of ordinary people.</div> </div> </div> </div>The literal core mechanic of Deviant as a gameline is that you need to obsessively pursue the ruination of someone or something \u2014 deserving or otherwise \u2014 or protect and serve someone with a probably-unhealthy level of devotion \u2014 ditto \u2014 in order to keep your soul from degenerating your existence in a variety of fun and awful ways, including paranoia, loss of empathy, escalatory murderous anger issues, splinter personalities, addiction to superpowers, and more. It is also a gameline where your specific supernatural powers <i>are</i> the majority of your template abilities and reproducing them is within the scope of an organization you may now or once have worked for or controlled, with a not-insubstantial amount of experimental-subject horror baked into the Origins and the examples of what conspiracies can be.<br /> <br /> &quot;Point-built powers-at-a-price on both sides of the Victor/Igor divide&quot; doesn't stop being a strong contender for the same headspace just because the base game supplies a unifying antagonist framework that gives you people who're easy to hate to draw Conviction Touchstones from; a game of Deviant can just as easily see Renegades tormenting people with no ties to the Web of Pain, just like you can run a Ghost Wolves game with no tribal interaction or an Uncalled game where your Messenger tries to lay low in an Infrastructure town.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And with Princess - well, the biggest knock on <i>that</i> fansplat is that it doesn't fit the Chronicles setting at all, and it's partly justified, too. Whereas Deviant, with its half-broken protagonists and occult conspirators with nefarious plans, is probably the official game closest to the tone of the original blue book. The only overlap I see is that both games can do some kinds of superhero stories, and even there the similarities aren't that close. </div> </div> </div>To repeat: Half of the gameline's core mechanic is having someone or several someones who you need to protect. The aesthetic breadth of Variations is such that &quot;you can manifest a magic sword at any time&quot; is a sample skinning of the basic Harmful Attack Power, and the breadth of Scars is such that you can have bad luck be the primary consequence of failing to treasure your relationships as a reincarnated psychic half-angel.<br /> <br /> Far be it from me to overplay the prominence of Pretty Cure in the genre, but when mahou shoujo now has sixteen generations of tokusatsu-adjacent material to work with it doesn't take a lot of effort to see &quot;evil corporation that makes kaijin&quot; and &quot;demonic otherworldly invaders and their legions of scrubs&quot; massaged into street-level conflicts between Guardians and the servants of the greater-scope elements of the Web of Pain. (Or, if that's not your bag, &quot;use your magic powers/try to resist using your magic powers to make your friends' lives easier&quot; is <i>also</i> an established subset of genre content.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T18:55:58-07:00","id":1460777,"title":"","content":"I would also add on the <b>Genius</b> point that <i>somebody</i> made the Deviants; and while the default assumption is that it was the work of a Conspiracy, that's not always the case. Sometimes, it's an individual. Though technically, that's more \u201cDeviant-adjacent\u201d than Deviant-proper \u2014 more like how ghosts don't have their own gameline in the Chronicles of Darkness, but exist in a Geist-adjacent role.<br /> <br /> And for <b>Princess</b>: technically, Buffy the Vampire Slayer could be treated as a Princess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-21-2021, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-21T22:08:47-07:00","id":1460788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1460777#post1460777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also add on the <b>Genius</b> point that <i>somebody</i> made the Deviants; and while the default assumption is that it was the work of a Conspiracy, that's not always the case. Sometimes, it's an individual. Though technically, that's more \u201cDeviant-adjacent\u201d than Deviant-proper \u2014 more like how ghosts don't have their own gameline in the Chronicles of Darkness, but exist in a Geist-adjacent role.<br /> <br /> And for <b>Princess</b>: technically, Buffy the Vampire Slayer could be treated as a Princess.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the continuing &quot;Deviant is great for Genius&quot; train, assuming that the Peerage is not a bunch of fuckwits being bad at their jobs*, the only reason they probably don't have an open ward of exploration on Divergence is some flashy but flimsy declarations of Obligation and being better than Lemuria, and as is probably have a great deal of exploration and creation of Deviants behind closed doors. THey're in good company with the Awakened on that one.<br /> <br /> That aside, while I'm not hard pressed to argue the Deviant model for Genius, it is also a interesting take and answers a lot. I feel like treating Genius's as a God-Machine and/or Divine Fire adjacent splat is probably still a better take, but no one says you can't ride the lightning between the lines.<br /> <br /> As for Magical Girls...................Woof, I could be here all day. I think I've actually already outlined a number of shows that easily adhere to Deviant model nicely, even going back to Sailor Moon (I'm not brave enough to try for Cutie Honey and the earlier models if for no other reason than I need that space of decent mass to codify the genre). All you need is a wiff of <i>possible</i> subversion and that stack of cards comes tumbling down. That Pretty Cure, as the continual generational definer of the genre, basically needs no translation to work in Deviant says <i>a lot</i>.<br /> <br /> *Look, I'm trying to give fair due after it, but I wrote 23,500+ words on why I don't like Genius, I don't just let that go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2021, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T09:25:56-07:00","id":1460854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1460777#post1460777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also add on the <b>Genius</b> point that <i>somebody</i> made the Deviants; and while the default assumption is that it was the work of a Conspiracy, that's not always the case. Sometimes, it's an individual. Though technically, that's more \u201cDeviant-adjacent\u201d than Deviant-proper \u2014 more like how ghosts don't have their own gameline in the Chronicles of Darkness, but exist in a Geist-adjacent role..</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Deviant-adjacent&quot; is exactly right. In Deviant you play a victim of mad science - even when your PCs did it to themselves. In Genius you play a perpetrator of mad science. Different perspective, leading to different conflicts, mood and themes. It's like putting the story of a military campaign as told by an officer in the victorious army and one told by a refugee from the battles in the same category because both of them are about &quot;war&quot;.<br /> <br /> With magical girls ... I do think the fact that magical girl antagonists are normally an otherworldly invading force, not other humans exploiting secret knowledge, distinguishes them from the stories that inspired Deviant. And while I can see, now, more similarities than I did at first, introducing that kind of antagonist would IMO shift the tone of the game. For instance, you'd lose the aspect of the PCs being fugitives, with only tenuous connections to mundane society. Fighting actual demons leaves a much better impression in the public eye than fighting Men in Black with secret nefarious intentions.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Devoted Companion will have tools for campaigns like that? Games with a &quot;good&quot; conspiracy fighting other conspiracies, possibly otherworldly, sounds like what we've been promised there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-22T10:59:47-07:00","id":1460871,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1336887-deviant-kickstarter?p=1337213#post1337213\">That one time I did a comparison for Magical Girls.<br /> <br /> EDIT:</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1460854#post1460854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Deviant-adjacent&quot; is exactly right. In Deviant you play a victim of mad science - even when your PCs did it to themselves. In Genius you play a perpetrator of mad science. Different perspective, leading to different conflicts, mood and themes. It's like putting the story of a military campaign as told by an officer in the victorious army and one told by a refugee from the battles in the same category because both of them are about &quot;war&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, taking into account that while the human basis for Divergence is a little rattled....<br /> <br /> Genius describes Inspiration as striking proto-Geniuses and warping them with insight into the Genius's they are, and sometimes a Genius can call it in by the depth of their obsession in pursuit of a project. Geniuses post-inspiration tend to fixate on the people who previously and currently get in the way of their projects, and at the same time can get obssessive about certain people appreciating. THe connection to the sciences they hyperfixate on can result in a nearly psychic and personal link to the subject matter, which is part of the way that Wonders can be generated in the way they are. And, of course, no result is repeatable.<br /> <br /> Sounds like a bunch of Autourgics, Genotyhpals, and Pathologicals Divergences into Cephalists, Chimerics, Invasives, and Coactives. Again, not a neat fit, but the initial comparison <i>does </i>have weight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2021, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T07:35:03-07:00","id":1461553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1459294#post1459294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Essence of Darkness.&quot; A lighter, more accessible variant of the CofD, streamlining and cutting mechanics and settings down to essential elements. Using Deviant's power building as a foundation and some of the other build-a-thing stuff, Contagion Chronicle crossover material, etc, to create a toolkit-approach-ground-up take on the core ideas of the CofD as a whole.<br /> <br /> By necessity you'd have to cut a lot of setting material to collapse everyone into a build-your-own-human-turned-monster-in-a-secret-occult-horror-world so I'd envision it as a sibling game line, quasi-separated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. Totally agree. I think we definitely need a more streamlined, lighter and uniformed toolkit approach for the whole CofD line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T08:55:23-07:00","id":1461559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1459294#post1459294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Essence of Darkness.&quot; A lighter, more accessible variant of the CofD, streamlining and cutting mechanics and settings down to essential elements. Using Deviant's power building as a foundation and some of the other build-a-thing stuff, Contagion Chronicle crossover material, etc, to create a toolkit-approach-ground-up take on the core ideas of the CofD as a whole.<br /> <br /> By necessity you'd have to cut a lot of setting material to collapse everyone into a build-your-own-human-turned-monster-in-a-secret-occult-horror-world so I'd envision it as a sibling game line, quasi-separated.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1461553#post1461553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Totally agree. I think we definitely need a more streamlined, lighter and uniformed toolkit approach for the whole CofD line.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason each gameline has its own systems that works in particular ways is because they are designed to facilitate certain themes, moods and stories that the games are about. Those things are the main identity of each game, with the game's monster type being chosen to fit that identity. If you remove the unique systems and replace it with generic systems that are supposed to fit multiple games, then you'll lose the identity of the <br /> I do absolutely think there's merit in a game that's about playing monsters just for the sake of playing monsters (and I do absolutely think a large part of CofD players play CofD games for this reason) but it'd lose out on the intended point of CofD games.<br /> <br /> The other option is to streamline each game individually* but then you end up with a dozen new books and that's a bad idea for several reasons.<br /> <br /> *The underlying system (Revised Storytelling System) is already hugely streamlined, so any attempts to streamline the actual Chronicles of Darkness game further would mostly just be removing any material you consider superfluous from the book. The only thing I'd rewrite are Merits to make them less fiddly, and reduce Conditions to an exhaustive but small list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T08:55:23-07:00","id":1461560,"title":"","content":"Edit: I believe this is the first time I've been subject to the double post bug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-30T07:02:31-07:00","id":1462126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1461559#post1461559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason each gameline has its own systems that works in particular ways is because they are designed to facilitate certain themes, moods and stories that the games are about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but there are some common through-lines in the CofD (the things that set it apart from the oWoD, for example) that could be highlighted for the relevant depth, and the Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle sets some foundational ideas I think could be extrapolated. Each of the individual game lines offers one or two design elements that could be carved out, as well. <br /> <br /> There's definitely a viable &quot;Essence of Darkness&quot; percolating in my subconscious that would make me very happy if it existed. Would I want it to replace the independent game line design for a more all-together-now approach? Probably not, but Exalted Essence isn't intended to replace Exalted either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T16:10:54-07:00","id":1462341,"title":"","content":"Another Mirrors Style Book would be awesome, and even better would be a fuller and cooler Space Opera/Cyberpunk book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-02T14:40:39-07:00","id":1462479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1461559#post1461559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason each gameline has its own systems that works in particular ways is because they are designed to facilitate certain themes, moods and stories that the games are about. Those things are the main identity of each game, with the game's monster type being chosen to fit that identity. If you remove the unique systems and replace it with generic systems that are supposed to fit multiple games, then you'll lose the identity of the.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. 2nd edition has put more effort into making the mechanics follow the themes and moods of the games. Haven't played it yet, but from what I see Promethean 2e is a great example of this.<br /> The thing is, this design is *<i>very</i>* oriented towards player characters and specific settings. It works great if you're a PC and play within that gameline's specific theme and setting.<br /> The need for a more streamlined system only arises with NPCs and crossovers.<br /> <br /> If you're running a Changeling chronicle and you want to introduce a Promethean NPC, you don't need to flesh out all its Pilgrimage and roles and whatever, just the basic information for personality and background. You could handle it the same way as Hunter does, with basically little more than Horrors rules and Dread Powers. So I guess a more streamlined system would be something somewhere between Horrors and fully-fleshed PC sheets as a toolkit for STs.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the problem doesn't come up if you only consider a single game line, but when you compare several it can be really annoying. For instance, the Integrity-like traits are supposed to be somewhat similar, or filling the same role, but they're completely different from each other. Yes, they're one of the main systems that provide unique identity and theme to each game line, but... come on, do they *<i>really</i>* need to have each a different dice roll for breaking points? Vampire rolls a fixed, decreasing dice pool based on a list of breaking points, Werewolf rolls Resolve + Composure, Changeling rolls an *<i>increasing</i>* dice pool + a roll for damage... ugh.<br /> (Speaking of which, there's a Changeling Contract that, when used against non-changelings, temporarily decreases the Integrity-equivalent trait. Which means that werwolves get shifted towards Spirit, Sin-Eaters lose their Supernatural Resistence trait, and Beasts... uhm, lose their Supernatural Resource I guess, or maybe they're immune? There's a lot of implications when considering Traits as equivalent but are actually very different. )<br /> Again, this is only a problem if you're considering crossovers.<br /> <br /> More in general, as it is I feel like CofD lacks uniformity and a sense of a global vision. You can find the same &quot;you go unnoticed and people ignore you&quot; power in Vampire Discipline, Werwolf Gift and Promethean Transmutation. There are also a lot of telepathic powers of some sort, that let you learn people's emotions, or Vices etc. that are quite similar to some degree. You might as well have a list of common supernatural powers in a Core rulebook and have each gameline reference them, or perhaps a common framework in the same vein as Twilight rules.<br /> If you want to make a new power that makes you immaterial, you only need five words: &quot;you enter Twilight [frequency] state&quot;. That's it. No need to describe every time how it works because it's a universal framework shared between all games. In the same way you could have a universal Telepathic powers framework etc.<br /> <br /> For example, the Variations Tags from Deviant, like Overt, Toggled etc. are a great instance of rules framework that could be applied uniformly to all games: activating the Celerity Discipline is Toggled and using Protean is Overt, stuff like that. Or the Krewe rules could be shared as a more general &quot;organizations&quot; rules for Vampire cults, Werewolf packs, Mage labyrinths etc. Do I really need to get a copy of Geist to have a cult system for my Vampire game?<br /> <br /> Anyway, apologies for the rant-ish post, and sorry if I'm deviating a bit from the actual thread. This topic would require a thread of its own.<br /> <br /> So, new book ideas. As far as classic horror tropes go, I think that Aliens may be one of the few left that could be explored in its own game line. Not sure how though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T00:59:01-07:00","id":1462527,"title":"","content":"I prefer the differences between how powers work for different splats but that\u2019s a personal thing. Not sure either how an Alien splat would work, but it definitely could if enough effort was put in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T09:57:40-07:00","id":1462663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1462479#post1462479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, apologies for the rant-ish post, and sorry if I'm deviating a bit from the actual thread. This topic would require a thread of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think your points are great for the thread on a possible 3rd edition, as at this point most of those changes would have to come from the ground, not a new book.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think a dedicated book for the ST should bring a more powerful &quot;Make-a-Monster&quot; tool. Something to handle a modular approach to stat building of NPCs with enough information where the ST want to go deep without the need for any information the ST deems irrelevant. The NPC must be able to bring some choice bits of thematic rules form their splat, for example, but without bringing all the rules. This isn't an easy proposal, but it is something the system currently lacks, the Horrors rules are on the right direction, but aren't enough yet.<br /> <br /> And it must be something able to discuss briefly several gameline themes so the ST can use them on their games without need for their actual books, as someone focused on running a single gameline is more likely to just not buy than to read through several other core books just for the sake of making NPCs. If well done this may even bring some players to buy the other books as they start to have enough experience with different things to want to try them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T10:31:54-07:00","id":1462670,"title":"","content":"If, hypothetically speaking, there was reason enough to reuse themes from existing games, I would be quite interested in new games based on Beast and Mummy.<br /> Beast has been badly hurt by its reputation, but it's also, in my personal opinion, not great mechanically speaking, and I also think a lot of people were disappointed by the &quot;type of monster&quot; was chosen for Beast.<br /> Certain design decisions, such as lack of gameplay loop outside of &quot;feeding leads to complications leads to Satiety expenditure leads to feeding&quot;, no organisational systems other than &quot;broods exists, have fun&quot; for a supposedly social splat, and a &quot;build a monster&quot; approach that is lackluster (especially after Deviant) all just don't mesh that well with me.<br /> The PCs being hosts to the psychic representations of monsters and can draw powers from them is kinda cool in its own way, but it definitely creates a disconnect between monster and PC. You can spend time and effort building a cool Pyramid Head knock-off PC to scare the shit out of people by invoking sirens and &quot;rustic&quot; architecture, but in actual play, it'll be your very human-looking PC posing as not!Pyramid Head. What I'd like to see is Boogeyman: The Spoopy where the character actually transforms into humankind's various fears and embody them more directly. Less Urged and more Claimed, basically.<br /> <br /> For Mummy, well, what I want is probably less a game that retreads the same themes and more a new core book that isn't stupidly opaque. It's like trying to read Werewolf except almost every single splat term is written in First Tongue with no English translations.<br /> Mechanically, it's also a bit wonky. Most of it doesn't concern me that much, but it's enough that my group refuses to play it even after shifting target numbers were removed so they won't get oWoD PTSD anymore.<br /> Edit: Basically, what I'm saying is that I'd like a game that's basically Mummy but actually disgestable and also playable for my group so I can actually play it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-04-2021, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T18:10:13-07:00","id":1464294,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this is spoken for in the thread or not but my dream chronicles gameline would be Wraith: (The Rising/The Restless/The Risen???).<br /> I would want it dove-tailed into Geist as much as possible. So much so that the two games or perhaps the two splats serve as an completely interconnected pair. Two core books two splats one gameline.<br /> <br /> I know second edition Geist put some word count towards making Ghosts playable but they deserve a full core book. It could go a long way towards fleshing out the cosmology of the underworld, the nature of death and what lies beyond. Of course a full book would expand and tighten up the mechanics of the restless dead. Not to mention it would help create a greater divide between the mechanical similarities between ghosts and spirits. I figure interconnecting a new Wraith to Geist would also elevate Geist, making it both more metaphysically relevant within the CoD and held in high esteem among Players and Stortellers<br /> And well I'm thinking on it, it couldn't hurt that Wraith: The Oblivion was such a well loved and critically acclaimed title. <br /> <br /> Also this is just a tiny detail i'd change; just refer to Plasm as Ectoplasm and naturally have It be the fuel for both Wraiths and Geists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:02:30-07:00","id":1464374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>basketcase</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1464294#post1464294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this is spoken for in the thread or not but my dream chronicles gameline would be Wraith: (The Rising/The Restless/The Risen???).<br /> I would want it dove-tailed into Geist as much as possible. So much so that the two games or perhaps the two splats serve as an completely interconnected pair. Two core books two splats one gameline.<br /> <br /> I know second edition Geist put some word count towards making Ghosts playable but they deserve a full core book. It could go a long way towards fleshing out the cosmology of the underworld, the nature of death and what lies beyond. Of course a full book would expand and tighten up the mechanics of the restless dead. Not to mention it would help create a greater divide between the mechanical similarities between ghosts and spirits. I figure interconnecting a new Wraith to Geist would also elevate Geist, making it both more metaphysically relevant within the CoD and held in high esteem among Players and Stortellers<br /> And well I'm thinking on it, it couldn't hurt that Wraith: The Oblivion was such a well loved and critically acclaimed title. <br /> <br /> Also this is just a tiny detail i'd change; just refer to Plasm as Ectoplasm and naturally have It be the fuel for both Wraiths and Geists</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh, I'd prefer the two to be separate gamelines. Wraith exploring 'civillised' ghost society (Shadowlands and Dark Kingdoms). While Geist explores the 'Barbaric' outskirts (Dead Dominions).<br /> <br /> I'd imagine the bound being quite unwelcome in the dark kingdoms (b/c if Wraiths start transcending far more easily. Where'd you find subjects to press under your thumb?) Infact, the Bound should seen as more of a myth than transcendence<br /> <br /> EDIT: On the other hand, geist could work as a sub-gameline of the hypothetical Nwod wraith like how you mentioned. Kinda like KOTE for V:TM (which I always thought of as a Wraoth sub-game).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","user":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","date":". 08-07-2022, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T10:30:24-08:00","id":1475912,"title":"","content":"Now, I've been working on a Pok\u00e9mon adaptation for several RPGs for some time now, a big personal project with a core, system-free set of principles and its application on some systems, starting by polishing my CofD one that I already STd some times. But I'm facing a writer's block already for months, despite most of it already being in place in my head.<br /> <br /> I decided then to present the document here already. It isn't yet what I wanted to bring, and even that would still be just a first draft. I would immensely appreciate any comment, critique and suggestion. Sometimes I do get lost in details and end up not following through my posited intentions in the first try, so I may need some reality checks too.<br /> <br /> The link follows, comments allowed:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18Vkw0QjJ95VQtm3COd5dwSp976AzYGB0vOo3FQr9kfE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T14:28:51-08:00","id":1475942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1475912#post1475912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I've been working on a Pok\u00e9mon adaptation for several RPGs for some time now, a big personal project with a core, system-free set of principles and its application on some systems, starting by polishing my CofD one that I already STd some times. But I'm facing a writer's block already for months, despite most of it already being in place in my head.<br /> <br /> I decided then to present the document here already. It isn't yet what I wanted to bring, and even that would still be just a first draft. I would immensely appreciate any comment, critique and suggestion. Sometimes I do get lost in details and end up not following through my posited intentions in the first try, so I may need some reality checks too.<br /> <br /> The link follows, comments allowed:<br /> <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/18Vkw0QjJ95VQtm3COd5dwSp976AzYGB0vOo3FQr9kfE/edit?usp=sharing&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Pokemon.<br /> Will read later \u2014 wonder if my past idlings of implementing them as spirit-based and \u2018lesser\u2019 Sin-Eaters could work here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T16:31:29-08:00","id":1476175,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for Dragon: The Ouroboros for a while, even had some drafts and themes.<br /> I love Beast and Requiem, both hit the themes of meaning and power in ways I love but I think Dragon could have some unique angles to explore those themes as the embodiment of power itself, now taking themes of self-destruction and obsession.<br /> Dragons would be born through Immolation, an act of self-birthing self-destruction where they burn their soul for power, substituting it for an ever-burning flame.<br /> The Hoard would be part of a dragon, their essence of being, the act of building it would be both satisfying the flame and self-justification for the right to power they hold and a way of giving them meaning within the community they share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","user":"LunaLupa","date":".  Edit: Grammar and better phrasing. 03-10-2022, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T19:59:29-08:00","id":1476186,"title":"","content":"Dragon the Ouroboros honestly sounds very interesting! What kind of powers would you give them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T03:49:37-08:00","id":1476200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1476186#post1476186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragon the Ouroboros honestly sounds very interesting! What kind of powers would you give them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had planned to divide the powers into Scales and Crowns, let me get my little draft.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Their power system would be based on Crowns the powers of the fire, the externalization of the internal flame, their imposition of rulership, and Scales the natural endowments of the dragon form. They are chosen differently. Crowns can be used in human or dragon form and they cost the Fuel Stat(maybe Embers?). Scales are just natural benefits that cost nothing to use in dragon form.<br /> For example Teeth Like Swords and Hide of Steel would be Scales, the first make your bite give 6L and don't need grapple to use, while the second gives you 5/5 armor, you just have this, no roll needed. Gleaming Eyes and Breath of Death would be Crowns, one that you have to roll Presence + Flame to supernaturally intimidate someone into a cowering animal, and the other you roll Dexterity + Flame to breath fire on someone.</div> <br /> Crown &amp; Scales would be acquired based on your Hoard, by acquiring new possessions you would acquire new powers, as the hoard would be the manifestation of a dragon's essence so an item that was robbed could grant the thief the Dragon's power(also send the dragon into murder rage as psychic-spiritual part of themselves was taken).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","user":"LunaLupa","date":".  Edit: Formatting 03-11-2022, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T06:13:26-08:00","id":1476205,"title":"","content":"Scales and Crowns are both pretty cool, like the divide between the two being passive and active powers. Also the fact these can be stolen makes them even more cool, with having to defend your Hoard from thieves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T07:19:10-08:00","id":1476206,"title":"","content":"Thieves were fun antagonists, I had made like 4 specific antagonist groups + other dragons, and I wanted all of them to tie with the themes of The Price of Power.<br /> Thieves would steal the Dragon's power for themselves and in many cases if they could kill the dragon in question become dragons themselves by consuming the Dragon's hoard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T16:29:28-08:00","id":1476238,"title":"","content":"If its not too much to ask, what were the Dragon\u2019s antag groups you came up with like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-21T19:13:27-07:00","id":1476912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1476238#post1476238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If its not too much to ask, what were the Dragon\u2019s antag groups you came up with like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes!<br /> Sorry for the long delay, I was busy with University stuff.<br /> <sup>I apologize for the bad text formating</sup> <div align=\"center\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><u>Chapter 6: Pit of Vipers</u><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>When the Cat's Away, the Mice will Play.</u></span></i></span></div></div> <div align=\"center\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">As the glory of a Lord spreads through the land, pretenders naturally rise to the occasion.</span></div></div> <div align=\"center\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Thieves:</span></u></span></div></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Mortals who in their arrogance and foolishness seek to take parts or the whole Hoard of a Dragon.<br /> Those who steal Treasures are granted part of the Dragon's power as they steal part of their very nature, many try to use this to even the odds on a fight agast the Dragon they stole it from in the hopes of taking their Hoard, though in most cases they just end up being swallowed whole by a furious Dragon instead.<br /> For this reason, Thieves rarely work alone, most of them work in bands fashioning themselves after dragon hunters and knights, many of those thieves' bands are led by CEOs, religious leaders, and others who already possess some form of power but still desire for more. Thieves rarely come from nowhere, many are part of professional groups who specialize in that or are even part of the Dragon's own Realm, working just like another servant while plotting to take his master's place. Many Dragons are especially cruel with Thieves, either because some consider it an unforgiving offense or because many of them became Dragons using similar methods and know the danger they pose.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Burnt:</span></u></span></div></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Ah yes, the sad fact of life is that it is a zero-sum game, for everyone who makes it, so many more don't. It's no different with the Lords, for every single Dragon who shed their human skin and consumed their soul in the Flame of power, so many more failed. Those who failed are the Burnt, those who when the moment of the consumption came hesitated, they did not fully commit to it, maybe they had doubts, maybe they were scared or simply changed their minds, sadly for them it was too late for that and the fire burned them fully, it consumed the soul and flesh and when it was over it just dimmed and faded. The Burnt have nothing to replace the souls but Cinder. They live to hunger for the taste of the primordial flame, searching for something to ignite the hollow on their souls, but their bodies can't hold the Flame's power. their flesh instead of shedding it fused, human and dragon, this made their burnt bodies inherently unstable, more they devour fire closer they are of losing control and become draconic abominations until their body explodes in fire and smoke; if they try to avoid eating fire, if they starve themselves, slowly the burn wounds spread across the skin until it consumes them whole transforming them in the dust.<br /> Many Dragons pity the Burnt, in them they see what they could have become if they didn't pay the full price, it tells them it was worth it or at least they believe so. Some Lords out of foolishness, kindness, or opportunism try to use the Burnt as servants, believing they can control them by supplying them with fire. Terrible misunderstanding about the nature of the Burnt, no fire will ever be enough for them, and beyond that, most of them are too unstable to be kept as trustworthy assets.<br /> The Burnt themselves carry a deep hatred for the Dragons.<br /> Many of them see the Lords as lucky bastards who got what they ever wanted, they envy what they almost could have, some even try to fashion themselves like a Dragon in an exercise of delusion. Some merely see Dragons as a ripe source for their<br /> so-needed fire and others hope that maybe by devouring the Dragon's fire whole they may have another chance...<br /> Burnt can use Scales but not Crowns.<br /> They also only have access to the half-dragon form.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Usurpers:</span></u></span></div></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">The most hated enemies of the Dragons, Usurpers are those mortals who in their arrogance have become obsessed with the Primordial Fire and so try to imitate it, those wannabe Prometheus seek to rob the Dragon of their Flame with the goal of recreating it on their own terms and using its power to achieve godhood. To the Dragon's contempt, the Usurpers study of the Flame had results, they were even capable of reproducing some of the Dragon's most valuable gifts: Crowns. Usurpers are capable of creating copies of Crowns and even their own Salamanders. Sadly for all their advances Usurpers rarely last long enough to achieve their dreams, most end devoured by dragons or killed by their own experiments. Usurpers rarely share their information with others they don't trust, this means Usurpers naturally end in either a lineage of master and apprentice or organized around a single figure that tends to make himself a cult leader.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Ashen Knights</span></u></span></div></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">The greatest enemies of the Dragons, and their arch-rivals. The Order of the Ashen Maiden tells a story about a woman, her name now lost in time but her deeds immortal, in her youth, she met a mighty cruel dragon and for the reason of vengeance or glory she decided to hunt the dragon herself. Against all expectation she survived every confrontation and by the end she was the one to give the last blown, she killed the dragon and so she sat tired contemplating her victory. As the night fell she found herself hungry, around the place there was no game to hunt and her provisions were over. &quot;What a joke, to kill a Dragon to die of starvation,&quot; she thought, but then she had an idea. Using her sword she opened the dragon's chest and took off the Dragon's heart. She quickly cooked the Heart and ate it. The heart tasted like ash but it filled her entirely, more than that it healed her wounds and filled her with a power she never had felt before. After that, she became known as the Ashen Maiden and became the first Dragon-Slayer.<br /> The Order is composed of those who wish to emulate the Maiden and so seek to kill dragons and devour their hearts. Some Knights do so out of a personal desire to take revenge on a dragon or hunt the most dangerous game, others do for the promise of power and immortality and others do so because they seek to embrace the strange powers discovered by the maiden.<br /> Similar to Dragons the Knights' soul was substituted for something else, but instead of the Flame, they have Ash, Ash grant the Knights powers similar to the Dragon but with key differences. Instead of Scales and Crown, they have Armor and Heart, Armor reflects their power of using the Ash to empower and build powerful weapons capable of killing dragons, their capacity of externalizing the Ash and infuse it on other objects or areas; Heart is their internal power, is the effects that grant them the power to heal or strengthen themselves and other similar passive physical powers.<br /> Like Dragons, they also use Embers but instead of spending Embers on non-physical powers like Crowns they use it on physical powers granted by the Heart.<br /> Knights don't have Hoard instead they have Oath. An Oath is what the Ash demands of a Knight, as their soul cracked and burned it became living Ash it demands a form to take and so it creates the Oath, the Oath can be any system of rules the Knight follows through their Oath they recover their Embers.<br /> Like dragons, they are immortal too.<br /> For this reason and other Dragons tend to see Knights as worthy opponents and rivals; many Dragons wasted centuries in an Ouroboros with an Ashen Knight, spending years and years of confrontations and destruction that end in nowhere. Many Dragons don't oppose working with Knights that are not targeting them specifically, seeing them as great allies to take down an enemy dragon; Knights who work with Dragons frequently are pejoratively called Riders by other Knights.<br /> Many Dragons seek to devour Knights because they make great trophies for their hoard and for a reason that is unknown to them devouring them empowers their Flame.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T00:11:10-07:00","id":1476923,"title":"","content":"Those antags are quite interesting, my favourites are definitely the Burnt &amp; the Ashen Knights. The chapter's name also fits very well for these groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-22T05:05:57-07:00","id":1476947,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah.<br /> Writing the Knights and the Burnt was a joy, I love them.<br /> <br /> Also thank you, I took a good time to find good names and quotes for the chapters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27153-lunalupa","name":"LunaLupa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27153_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T06:07:34-07:00","id":1478204,"title":"","content":"I would make a fantasy-based game where, rather than an x-splat and y-splat, you can choose different fantasy races and character classes. It would be a bit different from normal CoFD, so I don't think many people would be interested in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T08:35:28-07:00","id":1478216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1478204#post1478204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make a fantasy-based game where, rather than an x-splat and y-splat, you can choose different fantasy races and character classes. It would be a bit different from normal CoFD, so I don't think many people would be interested in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think a lot of people would be. Many of us also play other things like D&amp;D, and could be interested either for the rules hack or to actually use it depending on how you apply the specifics of the system to the idea to make for a new playing experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T13:09:35-07:00","id":1478233,"title":"","content":"Then it might not be such a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T20:12:38-07:00","id":1478252,"title":"","content":"That idea does sound very fascinating! What kind of powers would they have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T06:24:55-07:00","id":1478278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1459189-what-cofd-game-would-you-create?p=1478252#post1478252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That idea does sound very fascinating! What kind of powers would they have?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not entirely sure, but I have some ideas. To start off with the four standard fantasy classes:<br /> Fighters might be a bit like dark heroes with extra skill-related stuff. It would just be less broad and apply more to combat than other things.<br /> Clerics would be a bit like the the Malleus Maleficarum in terms of their powers.<br /> Wizards would probably be like mages except less overpowered. We might even be able to just take the magic system from Witch Finders and have that be it. Or maybe not.<br /> I have no clue what rogues would be like.<br /> <br /> For the standard fantasy races:<br /> I'd probably make elves be a bit like fairest changelings; though, I'm not entirely sure.<br /> The dwarves could be like wizened changelings; however, that wouldn't fit them 100%.<br /> I'm not sure about orcs or halflings.<br /> And these races wouldn't be full x-splats. They'd essentially give some minor advantages and drawbacks. I'd probably give humans minor advantages and drawbacks too, like they have in the Witcher tabletop rpg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T07:21:14-07:00","id":1478280,"title":"","content":"I think that selection works well enough. Have you thought up the enemies they will face?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T07:56:45-07:00","id":1478283,"title":"","content":"Well, if I had to guess, I'd say somewhat standard fantasy rpg enemies just to make things easier:<br /> Orcs or some similar race of beings<br /> Giants<br /> Dragons<br /> Wyverns<br /> Trolls<br /> Giant Spiders<br /> Undead<br /> Demons<br /> Etc.<br /> These could probably all be created using the Hunter: The Vigil monster creation system. Though, a few alterations might be made to make them fit the fantasy theme more. Like, if you want expendable bad guys that the characters can cut down in droves, maybe make them automatically fail all rolls to stay conscious? Or if you're making a boss monster, like an evil undead knight, that you want to have a lot of health, an option to give them an extra dot of health per potency point could be present. These could be put in as new dread powers and weaknesses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-08T12:37:15-07:00","id":1478291,"title":"","content":"I have a back-burner project I\u2019ve tinkered with for a few years of making Rise of the Guardians into a variant of the Purified: humans who were transformed into ephemeral beings through a profound act of their Virtue, and now seek to protect those ideals and guide society toward them - often becoming folk legends and mythic figures.<br /> Growing up on RotG and tNbC makes playing heroic holiday figures sound fun and nostalgic, but the concept can very quickly become appropriative and even blasphemous, so I keep setting it aside rather than get into the problematic weeds. The next time I pick it up, I might lean more heavily on inspiration like \u201cInk\u201d, or try moving the concept to an alt-Earth setting. But it keeps dipping into \u201cascension war\u201d themes, so it might not ever sit well with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T20:56:18-07:00","id":1478819,"title":"","content":"That's fair. That Purified variant sounds pretty interesting, hope you manage to iron it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}